(A) BUILD_EXIT=1 root cause — WinUI XAML markup-compiler crash (runner toolchain)
    C:\Users\...\microsoft.windowsappsdk.winui\2.1.0\buildTransitive\
      Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Markup.Compiler.interop.targets(847,9):
      Xaml Internal Error error WMC9999: Object reference not set to an instance of an object.
    The internal NRE cascades into ~120 spurious "WMC0001/WMC0110 Unknown type" errors for the
    app's OWN pre-existing C# controls (TsButton/TsBadge/TsCard/... in ComponentGallery.xaml,
    Styles.xaml, ShellWindow.xaml) — none authored or touched here. Reproduces on a clean
    obj/bin, single-threaded (-m:1) x64 build. The runner has NO Windows SDK installed
    (HKLM\...\Microsoft SDKs\Windows\v10.0 is empty), which the markup compiler requires.
    Microsoft.WindowsAppSDK has been pinned at 2.1.3 since the foundational commit 3709dd3c5
    (P0/0003, 2026-06-04); the sibling surface GuardMode (0054) logged BUILD_EXIT=0 against that
    same pin, so this is a runner-environment regression, not a repo or surface defect.

(B) TEST_EXIT=1 root cause — pre-existing integration-branch source collision + absent UI runner
    1) The headless test assembly (TeslaSync.App.Tests, net10.0) fails to COMPILE due to a
       duplicate-type collision predating this surface:
         EnergyFlowWidget\EnergyFlowWidget.Model.cs and
         EnergyFlowAnimatedWidget\EnergyFlowAnimatedWidget.Model.cs
       both declare EnergyFlowState / EnergyFlowSnapshot / EnergyFlowSize / ... in the SAME
       namespace TeslaSync.App.DashboardWidgets (CS0101 / CS0111 / CS8863); FleetStats repeats the
       pattern (FleetStatsResultMapper). Both widget files predate 0064 and are outside scope.
    2) The TeslaSync.App.UITests assembly hard-fails (WinAppDriver/Appium runner absent on
       http://127.0.0.1:4723/), the same platform-capability gap the sibling surfaces record.

